{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Scheduling a Meeting"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Continuous "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The Present Continuous tense is formed by \u201cbe\u201d and the present participle (-ing) of a verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> tense is normally used to talk about an action happening in the present or at the moment. However, it can also be used to indicate future. It basically expresses the idea that something will (or will not) happen in the future. The future can be noticed through the use of a future word."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Spoken English</span><br/> The <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> tense is very common in Spoken English. Below you will find a list with the most common verbs used with the <span class=\"strong\">Present continuous</span> in spoken English. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ol><li>going</li><li>saying</li><li>doing</li><li>trying</li><li>talking</li><li>looking</li><li>telling</li><li>asking</li><li>getting</li><li>being</li></ol>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">m</span> just stopp<span class=\"strong\">ing</span> by to say hi. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">m</span>  talk<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>  with my mom on Skype. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">m</span>  hav<span class=\"strong\">ing</span> a meeting with Fernando <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"strong\">at 3 pm. </span></span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking When People are Free"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " It is important to enquire when you want to find out about someone's availability. Here are some phrases you can use: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":6,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm just</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">dropping by<br/>  stopping by</span></span\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">see<br/> check</span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> when you're</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">free.<br/> available. </span></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you mind ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">wait<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing </span>until after lunch?<br/> meet<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> in the afternoon?<br/> talk<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ing</span> tomorrow?</span >\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The adjective \u2018available' (used before a noun) is commonly used in the following patterns when asking about people's availability."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">be + available + to + verb<br/>  \t</span>Would you <span class=\"strong\">be available to</span> meet after lunch?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">be + available + for + noun / -ing</span> <br/> \tWould you <span class=\"strong\">be available for</span> a coffee after the meeting? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">be + readily / freely / easily / widely available</span><br/>  \tI <span class=\"strong\">am easily available for </span>a coffee in the late<br/>           afternoon.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drop by"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make a short visit somewhere"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm just dropping by to see how you're doing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when scheduling a meeting. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "see when you're free"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to check when someone is available"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was hoping to see when you're free for our meeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take the week off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop working for a period of one week"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was hoping I would take the week off. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob09aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pressing responsibilities"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very important duties you need to deal with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm glad you can keep up with some pressing responsibilities."}, {"type": "audio", "c